segments.text:
And as touching praiers,
Ezechias was heard, when he praied with wéeping; and death being ſhewed vnto him, was deferred vntill another time. Ioſias likewiſe was heard,
who praied vnto God with manie teares. The 126. pſalme ſpeaketh thus of the fruit of praier, which hath ſorrowe and teares ioined therewith;
They went and wept, caſting their ſeeds, but doubtleſſe they ſhall come againe, and with ioie ſhall bring their ſheaues with them. And they which ſowe in teares, ſhall reape in ioie. It is alſo written in the ſixt pſalme;
The Lord hath heard the voice of my weeping. And in the 56. pſalme;
The teares of the ſaints are as it were put in a pot or bottle before God, and faithfullie ſealed in his booke.
Dauid alſo in the 95. pſalme ſtirreth vs vp by theſe words; Let vs weepe before the Lord that made vs, &c. But much more are we ſtirred vp thervnto by the example of Chriſt; who (as it is written in the epiſtle to the Hebrues) With a lowd crie,
and with teares praied for vs.
Paule alſo, in the 20. chapter of the Acts ſaith, that he had long ſerued the Lord with an humble hart, and with teares.
